1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Follow Ava and Leo through durable memory, governed learning,
accessible routing, transactional play, GraphRAG, and
consented AR memory.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Begin Ava's visit: Click Reset, then Retain. Ava requests a
quiet, mobility-friendly visit. Agent Memory stores messages
and typed memories with embeddings, showing durable semantic
and episodic memory.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
retain() creates Ava's thread, stores the conversation,
extracts typed records, and adds the earlier rainy-visit
episode.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Conversation rows and durable memory rows are added. Each
memory carries identity scope, metadata, and an embedding for
later retrieval.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Personalize Ava's plan: Click Recall + Reuse. Scoped search
retrieves Ava's breakfast, accessibility, entertainment, and
prior-visit memories. Oracle AI Database ranks relevant
records, showing scope before similarity.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
recall() applies exact guest, agent, and thread scope before
search ranking, then assembles the selected memories into
reusable context.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The database reads Ava-scoped active records and ranks them by
relevance. Recall is read-only, so no stored row changes.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Correct Ava's preference: Click Refine. Ava clarifies that she
prefers the lantern show, not fireworks. The memory is updated
while retaining provenance, demonstrating correction rather
than silently preserving misinformation.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
correct() finds the inaccurate record and calls the memory
update operation with the corrected preference and correction
provenance.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
The active memory content and metadata change from fireworks
to the lantern show while retaining its durable record
identity and provenance.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Forget tonight's closure: Click Expire. The temporary
garden-path closure becomes ineligible for future recall. TTL
distinguishes short-lived operational conditions from Ava's
durable accessibility and entertainment preferences.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
expire() updates the temporary closure's expiration metadata,
then verifies that normal search excludes the now-expired
operational memory.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The closure row remains available for evidence, but its
expiration state makes it ineligible for future active-memory
searches.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Learn from rainy visits: Click Dream. Three successful
covered-route experiences produce a candidate rainy-evening
rerouting guideline. Episodic traces become generalized
procedural memory without copying private visitor details.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
dream() recalls three successful de-identified traces and
writes one generalized pending guideline without copying
visitor-specific facts.

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Three trace memories remain separate. A new pending guideline
records the generalized rainy-evening rerouting procedure and
source count.

17
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Govern the lesson: Click Approve. A reviewer activates the
rerouting guideline and records approval metadata. Human
oversight prevents automatically inferred procedures from
silently influencing future visitors.

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:13,000
approve() updates only the pending guideline, adding approved
status, reviewer identity, and approval time before shared
reuse is allowed.

19
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The guideline's metadata changes from pending to approved.
Reviewer and timestamp provenance make the governance decision
inspectable.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Help Leo safely: Click Next guest. Leo encounters similar rain
and receives the approved rerouting procedure, but none of
Ava's private preferences. Shared learning remains separate
from personal memory.

21
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:35,000
next_day() proves Leo's private scope cannot read Ava's
records, then separately retrieves the approved shared
guideline.

22
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:42,000
The database performs two scoped reads and changes no rows.
Leo sees the approved lesson, while Ava's personal records
remain outside his scope.

23
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Prepare Memory Quest: Click Reset quest. Ava's previous
progress, points, badge, and reward history disappear, while
the park map, paths, clues, and quest definitions remain
reusable.

24
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:57,000
reset() deletes only visitor-specific quest results in
dependency-safe order and preserves the reusable park world
and knowledge.

25
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Progress, badge, and reward-audit tables become empty. Places,
paths, quests, clues, graph relationships, and knowledge
remain intact.

26
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Plan Ava's accessible route: Click Plan route. Property Graph
finds connected accessible paths; Oracle Spatial measures
physical distance. Ava avoids Summit Steps and travels through
covered, step-free locations.

27
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:19,000
plan() filters graph edges for open accessible paths, computes
the permitted route, and asks Oracle Spatial for straight-line
distance.

28
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:26,000
This is a read-only planning step. Graph topology supplies
traversable paths and Spatial geometry supplies physical
separation; no rows change.

29
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Form the quest party: Click Start quest. Ava and Leo join
Covered Constellations through consent-bounded party
relationships. Transactional progress and audit rows start
without combining their private memories.

30
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:41,000
start() validates the consented party and inserts quest
progress plus the start audit event in one transaction.

31
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:48,000
A progress row starts at step zero with zero points, and a
QUEST_STARTED audit row records the same committed
transaction.

32
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Find the breakfast clue: Click Complete checkpoint. Ava
reaches Quiet Café and earns 50 points. The database
atomically updates progress and audit evidence, preventing
reward inconsistencies.

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:03,000
complete_next_step() locks Ava's progress, validates the next
ordered checkpoint, adds 50 points, and writes the checkpoint
audit atomically.

34
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Progress advances to Quiet Cafe with 50 points. The matching
CHECKPOINT_COMPLETED audit row records the same 50-point
delta.

35
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Discover the atrium mosaic: Click Complete checkpoint again.
Ava follows the covered connector to the constellation
artwork. Another transaction validates sequence, records the
checkpoint, and awards 50 points.

36
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:25,000
The same transaction boundary validates checkpoint two,
advances progress in sequence, adds 50 points, and appends
audit evidence.

37
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Progress advances to Covered Atrium with 100 total points. A
second checkpoint audit row proves the ordered state
transition.

38
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Finish at Lantern Garden: Click Complete checkpoint a third
time. Ava decodes the founder symbol, completes the quest,
reaches 400 points, and receives the Lantern Pathfinder badge
transactionally.

39
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:47,000
The final checkpoint transaction completes progress, awards
the completion bonus, issues the badge, and records the final
audit event together.

40
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Ava's progress is completed at 400 points and the Lantern
Pathfinder badge row is added without any partial reward
state.

41
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Expand the park story: Click Retrieve + expand. Vector Search
finds quiet, rainy, accessible lore; Property Graph connects
it to places, paths, and quests. GraphRAG explains
relationships beyond similarity.

42
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:09,000
graph_rag() embeds the question, ranks grounded knowledge by
vector distance, and expands each hit through explicit graph
relationships.

43
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:16,000
This is a read-only retrieval step. Native vectors find
semantic matches, while graph tables supply connected places,
paths, and quest context.

44
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Remember through AR: Configure consent, start an AR session,
then confirm 'remember this.' The simulated glasses show route
overlays while Agent Memory stores Ava's observation with
guest scope, provenance, and TTL.

45
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:31,000
start_session() fixes privacy choices for the session.
remember() stores only the confirmed observation with guest
scope, AR provenance, and bounded retention.

46
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:38,000
The session and consent state are recorded, the observation
becomes expirable guest memory, and the AR audit captures the
authorized action.

47
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Search opted-in media: Enable recording consent, index the
atrium caption, then search for the constellation artwork.
Oracle AI Database filters identity, consent, and expiration
before vector ranking.

48
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:53,000
remember_media() indexes the consented description.
search_media() filters guest, agent, thread, consent, and TTL
before vector-distance ranking.

49
00:05:53,000 --> 00:06:00,000
The media description, native vector, consent provenance, and
expiration are stored. Scoped search returns one eligible
constellation-mosaic result.

50
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:09,000
The experience combines scoped memory, human governance,
graph, Spatial, vectors, transactions, gamification, and
privacy-first AR without retraining model weights.
